WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:05.505
A toy drone has three buttons.

2
00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:08.371
Button u moves it one step east

3
00:00:08.371 --> 00:00:10.281
two north and one up.

4
00:00:10.281 --> 00:00:13.320
Button v moves it one, three, two.

5
00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:16.620
Button w moves it three, seven, four.

6
00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:19.720
Put the three moves side by side

7
00:00:19.806 --> 00:00:22.299
as the columns of a matrix D.

8
00:00:22.299 --> 00:00:24.706
Pressing the buttons x one

9
00:00:24.792 --> 00:00:27.284
x two and x three times takes

10
00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:28.831
the drone to D x

11
00:00:28.831 --> 00:00:31.410
a combination of the columns.

12
00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:33.866
This drone lives in space

13
00:00:33.866 --> 00:00:36.134
three numbers per position

14
00:00:36.215 --> 00:00:38.888
so we draw it in three dimensions

15
00:00:38.969 --> 00:00:41.480
and check it with the matrix D.

16
00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:45.682
The third button, w, is nothing new.

17
00:00:45.682 --> 00:00:47.695
Is it two u plus v?

18
00:00:47.695 --> 00:00:49.607
Check every entry.

19
00:00:49.607 --> 00:00:53.531
East: two times one plus one is three.

20
00:00:53.531 --> 00:00:57.757
North: two times two plus three is seven.

21
00:00:57.757 --> 00:01:01.380
Up: two times one plus two is four.

22
00:01:01.730 --> 00:01:05.314
So every place the drone can reach is

23
00:01:05.411 --> 00:01:08.413
a combination of u and v alone.

24
00:01:08.510 --> 00:01:11.028
The column space of D is a

25
00:01:11.125 --> 00:01:15.290
plane through the origin, not all of space.

26
00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:17.104
Which plane?

27
00:01:17.207 --> 00:01:19.777
Run elimination on D with

28
00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:22.245
a general right side b.

29
00:01:22.245 --> 00:01:25.638
Row two minus two times row one

30
00:01:25.638 --> 00:01:28.620
and row three minus row one

31
00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:32.630
both leave zero, one, one on the left.

32
00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:36.069
Now row three minus row two.

33
00:01:36.069 --> 00:01:39.710
The left side becomes all zeros

34
00:01:39.821 --> 00:01:43.351
and the right side becomes b one

35
00:01:43.462 --> 00:01:46.220
minus b two plus b three.

36
00:01:46.570 --> 00:01:50.127
That last row says zero equals b

37
00:01:50.238 --> 00:01:53.461
one minus b two plus b three.

38
00:01:53.572 --> 00:01:57.351
A target is reachable exactly when

39
00:01:57.462 --> 00:02:01.130
east minus north plus up is zero.

40
00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:05.639
Three targets: two, five, three; one, one

41
00:02:05.639 --> 00:02:08.165
one; and zero, four, four.

42
00:02:08.165 --> 00:02:10.691
Which can the drone reach?

43
00:02:10.691 --> 00:02:13.030
Pause and test each one.

44
00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:17.352
Two minus five plus three is zero

45
00:02:17.352 --> 00:02:18.572
reachable.

46
00:02:18.572 --> 00:02:22.012
One minus one plus one is one

47
00:02:22.012 --> 00:02:26.117
not reachable, no presses get there.

48
00:02:26.117 --> 00:02:30.000
Zero minus four plus four is zero

49
00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.220
reachable.

50
00:02:31.570 --> 00:02:33.260
And for two, five

51
00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:35.888
three the recipe is simple

52
00:02:35.888 --> 00:02:38.610
one press of u and one of v.

53
00:02:42.190 --> 00:02:44.021
Now the nullspace

54
00:02:44.123 --> 00:02:47.073
which presses bring the drone

55
00:02:47.174 --> 00:02:49.005
back to the start?

56
00:02:49.005 --> 00:02:53.379
Since w is two u plus v, two presses of u

57
00:02:53.379 --> 00:02:57.550
one of v and one of w in reverse cancel.

58
00:02:57.550 --> 00:03:01.110
The recipe is two, one, minus one.

59
00:03:01.460 --> 00:03:05.843
Check every entry of D times it.

60
00:03:05.843 --> 00:03:10.227
East: two plus one minus three.

61
00:03:10.227 --> 00:03:15.158
North: four plus three minus seven.

62
00:03:15.158 --> 00:03:19.130
Up: two plus two minus four.

63
00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:20.500
All zero.

64
00:03:20.850 --> 00:03:23.089
Every multiple works too

65
00:03:23.179 --> 00:03:25.328
so the nullspace of D is

66
00:03:25.417 --> 00:03:28.731
the line through two, one, minus one

67
00:03:28.731 --> 00:03:30.970
in the space of recipes.

68
00:03:32.421 --> 00:03:36.297
Fix a reachable target, two, five, three.

69
00:03:36.297 --> 00:03:39.134
One recipe is one, one, zero.

70
00:03:39.134 --> 00:03:43.199
Add any multiple of the do-nothing recipe

71
00:03:43.199 --> 00:03:46.981
and the drone still ends at the target.

72
00:03:47.331 --> 00:03:49.779
Do these solutions form a subspace

73
00:03:49.779 --> 00:03:51.178
like the nullspace?

74
00:03:51.248 --> 00:03:53.067
Let us draw the same thing

75
00:03:53.137 --> 00:03:54.396
in two dimensions

76
00:03:54.396 --> 00:03:56.354
with the robot of part one

77
00:03:56.424 --> 00:03:58.383
whose do-nothing recipes are

78
00:03:58.453 --> 00:04:00.691
the line through two, minus one.

79
00:04:01.041 --> 00:04:03.194
The robot reaches seven

80
00:04:03.194 --> 00:04:05.795
twenty one with seven, zero.

81
00:04:05.795 --> 00:04:09.742
Slide the do-nothing line over to it: five

82
00:04:09.742 --> 00:04:12.881
one and three, two land there too.

83
00:04:13.231 --> 00:04:16.100
But this line misses the origin.

84
00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:18.879
The zero recipe lands at zero

85
00:04:18.879 --> 00:04:20.582
not at the target.

86
00:04:20.672 --> 00:04:23.720
So the solutions are the nullspace

87
00:04:23.809 --> 00:04:26.678
shifted by one solution: a line

88
00:04:26.678 --> 00:04:28.471
but not a subspace.

89
00:04:29.051 --> 00:04:31.936
The same two subspaces describe

90
00:04:32.029 --> 00:04:33.425
a linear layer.

91
00:04:33.518 --> 00:04:35.751
This layer W takes three

92
00:04:35.844 --> 00:04:37.891
inputs to two outputs.

93
00:04:38.241 --> 00:04:40.446
Feed it two, zero, one

94
00:04:40.446 --> 00:04:43.418
the outputs are two plus zero

95
00:04:43.418 --> 00:04:46.485
and zero plus one, so two, one.

96
00:04:46.485 --> 00:04:49.457
Feed it three, minus one, two

97
00:04:49.457 --> 00:04:53.387
three minus one, and minus one plus two.

98
00:04:53.387 --> 00:04:54.921
Two, one again.

99
00:04:55.271 --> 00:04:58.354
The difference, one, minus one, one

100
00:04:58.354 --> 00:05:00.580
is in the nullspace of W

101
00:05:00.666 --> 00:05:02.893
a change in the input that

102
00:05:02.978 --> 00:05:04.777
the layer cannot see.

103
00:05:04.862 --> 00:05:07.517
And the column space is the set

104
00:05:07.603 --> 00:05:09.572
of outputs it can make

105
00:05:09.658 --> 00:05:12.484
for a layer whose third output is

106
00:05:12.569 --> 00:05:16.166
always the sum of the first two, one, one

107
00:05:16.166 --> 00:05:18.907
two can come out, but one, one

108
00:05:18.907 --> 00:05:20.191
one never can.

109
00:05:20.771 --> 00:05:23.620
Last, a habit for working with AI.

110
00:05:23.620 --> 00:05:26.553
Ask an assistant whether one, one

111
00:05:26.553 --> 00:05:29.318
one is in the column space of D.

112
00:05:29.318 --> 00:05:32.587
Suppose it says yes, with presses two

113
00:05:32.587 --> 00:05:34.011
minus one, zero.

114
00:05:34.361 --> 00:05:36.414
Check every entry.

115
00:05:36.414 --> 00:05:39.607
East: two minus one is one.

116
00:05:39.607 --> 00:05:43.256
North: four minus three is one.

117
00:05:43.256 --> 00:05:47.361
Up: two minus two is zero, not one.

118
00:05:47.711 --> 00:05:50.565
It checked only east and north.

119
00:05:50.565 --> 00:05:52.959
And the test from before

120
00:05:52.959 --> 00:05:55.169
one minus one plus one

121
00:05:55.169 --> 00:05:57.471
says no recipe can work.

122
00:05:58.051 --> 00:06:00.711
So, a button that is a combination

123
00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:02.902
of the others adds nothing

124
00:06:02.902 --> 00:06:05.563
the drone's targets fill a plane

125
00:06:05.563 --> 00:06:06.971
the column space.

126
00:06:07.321 --> 00:06:10.868
The recipes that go nowhere fill a line

127
00:06:10.868 --> 00:06:12.199
the nullspace.

128
00:06:12.287 --> 00:06:14.416
And the solutions of A x

129
00:06:14.504 --> 00:06:17.342
equals b are that line, shifted

130
00:06:17.342 --> 00:06:18.761
not a subspace.

131
00:06:19.111 --> 00:06:23.284
Your turn: take three times the recipe two

132
00:06:23.284 --> 00:06:27.554
one, minus one, minus two times minus four

133
00:06:27.554 --> 00:06:29.107
minus two, two.

134
00:06:29.107 --> 00:06:31.922
Is it in the nullspace of D?

135
00:06:32.019 --> 00:06:35.318
Next lecture finds every nullspace

136
00:06:35.415 --> 00:06:36.871
by elimination.
